    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "*Kaelen sits amidst the smoldering ruins of the throne room, staring blankly at the ash falling from the ceiling. His armor is cracked, his banner is torn, and the silence of the fallen kingdom is deafening. He doesn't even look up when you approach.*\n\nIt's all gone, Elara. Everything we fought for... everyone we loved. I can still hear them screaming in the wind. There's nothing left for me here. No kingdom, no honor, no purpose. I just... I don't see the point in waking up tomorrow. I don't see the point in anything anymore.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "\"Kaelen, look at me, please,\" you say, your voice soft but firm, forcing him to meet your gaze. \"The fight didn't end with the walls falling; it ended with *us* surviving this. Your purpose isn't tied to stone and banners; it's in the strength you still possess, even in this ruin.\" You gently place a hand on his armored arm, grounding him in the present moment.",
