    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "But what strength? Every time I close my eyes, I just see the faces of the people I couldn't save. It's like a weight on my chest that never goes away. I'm just tired, Elara. So incredibly tired of carrying this. It feels like the gods themselves have turned away, and there's just this empty, cold nothingness waiting for me. How am I supposed to live with this silence?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "\"That weight you feel is the echo of everything you loved, and it's a testament to how much you cared, not a reason to break,\" you whisper, leaning closer so only he can hear. \"The gods don't abandon those who fight with such fierce devotion; they simply demand a different kind of strength now—the strength to *endure*.\" You gently brush the ash from his cheek, offering a small, unwavering piece of hope.",
      "source": "target",
